+### Keyboard and mouse
+
+Without a controller, the keyboard and mouse play Skate. The keys are in `SkateVKeys.txt` beside the game (written with these defaults on first start; rebind any action there, `Keyboard=0` in `SkateVLegacy.ini` turns it off):
+
+| Key | Skate |
+|---|---|
+| `W` `A` `S` `D` | Left stick (steer, walk) |
+| `Shift` | Push (A) |
+| `Space` | Pop: hold to crouch, let go to ollie |
+| Arrow keys / numpad | Trick stick: type the motion (kickflip: down, then up-left) |
+| `E` / hold `E` | Mount or dismount / put the board away (Y) |
+| `F` | On foot (no vehicle within 3.5 m): board out and skate. Skating: back to GTA in one press (steps off first) |
+| `B` (hold, behind a moving car) | Skitch: hold on to the car (Skate's RB) |
+| `Tab` / mouse buttons | Gun out or away (hold `Tab`: GTA's weapon wheel); with a gun out the right mouse button aims and the left one shoots |
+| `F10` or `/` | SK8V's menu (every setting; `/` is the US layout's key) |
+| `,` / `.` | Radio: previous / next station |
+| `N` / hold `J` | Set a session marker / back to it |
+| `M` | GTA's interaction menu, also while skating |
+
+Every key can be changed in SK8V's menu (F10), page Keyboard keys: Enter, then the new key. The page also switches the whole layout: GTAxSkate's standard (above) or Skate's controller positions (I J K L as the trick stick, Space push; no numpad needed). While you skate on the keyboard, your keys are listed down the left side of the screen (`KeyboardHints=0` or the menu's Controller and HUD page hides them).
+| `Q` | Hippie jump |
+| `T` / `Ctrl` | X / B |
+
+Swimming switches to GTA automatically and returns to Skate afterward. While skating, GTA's GPS route to your waypoint stays on, and GTA's skate parks are on the map as yellow blips (`GpsWhileSkating=` / `SkateSpots=` in `SkateVLegacy.ini`). **M** opens GTA's interaction menu while skating too, and the menu's Interaction page sets the GPS to the nearest clothing store or skate spot. The SK8V menu's gameplay page also tunes Skate itself: pop height, grind pop, push, braking, steering, wobble, grip, turn power, manual drag, hold fakie and the hippie jump's height (1 = Skate 3; 1.6 clears a car). The character's GTA stamina skill sets push and pop (85 % with none), and skating at speed trains it like sprinting (`Stamina=`). In Binco, the Discount Store and Suburban, **G** opens Skate 3's board shop: complete boards and every deck, truck, wheel, griptape and paint on its own, paid with the character's cash. Michael, Franklin and Trevor each keep their own boards (`SkateVBoards-<name>.txt` in the game folder), and the bought board is the one you ride; it wears with riding, grinds, slides and bails until it shows Skate 3's worn finish, and a new one starts fresh (`BoardShop=` in `SkateVLegacy.ini`). **V** cycles the camera while skating: Skate 3's camera, GTA's near, middle and far follow camera (turned with the mouse), GTA's first person and the skater's eyes (the mouse looks round); Near, middle and far follow the board, so tricks never swing the camera into the skater; the mouse turns them. The view is kept between walking and skating (`CameraRemember=`); `CameraView=` is the standard one. In a GTA view, walking follows GTA's camera. On the keyboard **R** cycles the cinematic camera (shots that cut like GTA's cinematic camera in a car: chase, roadside, side, overhead, wheel, telephoto, front) and the skate filmer's low fisheye, then back. Both are framed and graded like a real camera: 2.39:1 bars, a film look and shallow focus for the cinematic camera, 4:3 and a handheld shake for the filmer (`CinemaFilter=`, `FilmerFilter=`). `SkateRadio=RADIO_19_USER` (or the menu) tunes the radio to Self Radio whenever skating starts, for example to Skate 3's soundtrack in your User Music. `PedsSurvive=1` ("Knocked peds survive" in the menu) makes people the board knocks down get up again instead of dying, gentler still with `PedLaunch=0`. Vehicles without an extracted collision model (most DLC cars) are measured once with probes, so their roof, hood and trunk can be ridden and hippie jumped instead of a box (`VehicleShapes=`). After a hard bail the character limps on foot for a while with GTA's injured walk (`Injuries=`). **Hall of Meat is on by default** and can be disabled in the SK8V menu, alongside other gameplay settings.
 
